From 65a4e1ca528900a7ae8e6ed3dc3c72bfed9508b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/90] java mods: structure templates brought up to date are
 kept on disk

Mods ship structure templates from many older DataVersions, and each was updated by DataFixerUpper whenever it was loaded (the bridge also lets the fixer's rule caches go every few chains, to bound its memory): hundreds of ms a template on the worldgen threads while flying (UMP stack samples: DataFixTypes.update under TemplateSource.readStructure). TemplateSource.readStructure's update now goes through HorizonTemplateCache: the updated tag is kept in <bridge work>/template-cache/<data version>/ by the SHA-256 of the original, so a template is updated once. Current templates are untouched; anything that fails falls back to the fixer. The JVM gets the work folder as -Dhorizon.work.

UMP perf_test, 100 mods, LOD 512, second run with the cache: Java mirror tick 345 ms in the worldgen peak (was 700-990), structure_references 165 ms each (was 440-640), far terrain filled in 107 s (was 164-194); 205 templates cached (1 MB). 75/75 tests.
